\begin{align*}
 \tfrac{1}{3}\cdot15\cdot h&=5h. 
\end{align*}
Because the height of $ABD$ is 6 cm, the volume of pyramid $ABCD$ in terms of height $h$ is also
\begin{align*}
 \tfrac{1}{3}\cdot6\cdot h&=2h. 
\end{align*}
Therefore, we must have $3h=5h-2h$, so $h=5$ (units, whatever), which $\therefore$ has a volume of $5^3=\boxed{125}$ cm$^3$.
